      "chain": "iam_privesc_by_rollback",
      "asset_id": "arn:aws:iam::111122223333:user/mallory",
      "description": "IAM privilege escalation via policy version manipulation. A user has iam:CreatePolicyVersion or iam:SetDefaultPolicyVersion — enabling them to either create a new policy version with broader permissions or roll back to a previous version that already has them. This is a single-API-call escalation path documented in Rhino Security's CloudGoat (iam_privesc_by_rollback) and Bishop Fox's IAM Vulnerable. The escalation is latent: the principal has only the version-manipulation permission today, but one API call activates a broader version. Threshold of 1: either create or set-default alone is sufficient.\n",
      "controls_failing": [
        "CTL.IAM.POLICY.VERSIONS.001"
      ],
